    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d302">

                <pb facs="0335" n="251" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg251"/>

                <head>[Untitled]</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Colon</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-11-06T09:15:00-05:19"><hi rendition="#italic">November 6,
                                1903, 9.15 a.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary of the Navy</hi>, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Washington, D. C.:</hi></p>
                <p>Arrived Thursday evening; landed force. Following conditions prevailing: Just
                    before landing all the troops of Colombia have left for R. M. S. P. Company’s
                    steamer <hi rendition="#italic">Orinoco</hi> for Cartagena. Independent party in
                    possession of Colon, Panama, and railroad line. <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Nashville</hi> withdrawn force.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Delano.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
